{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>We shall not strike him down fatally.</b> The brothers' counsel was grievous to Reuben, and his intention was to save him. Had he said simply ״we shall not strike him down״ without more, he would have shown by his words that his objection was from compassion for him. Therefore he added the word נפש — meaning that his concern was not for Joseph but for them: that they should not strike down any person's life. And likewise what he said, ״Do not shed blood,״ and did not say ״his blood״ — meaning: I too, like you, hated him, and I am not concerned for his blood at all, but only for you, that you not become shedders of blood."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:18.205086118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}